  "expected_answer": "functional skipped (signed-in check), context pass, load pass, accessibility FAIL: brand colour #FFE680 on white has a contrast of about 1.3:1, needs 4.5:1; responsiveness not run (pending). alpha_app is now reverted and a fix task was filed.",
  "final_text": "The tests failed. alpha_app is now marked **reverted**, so it goes back to you before anything else happens to it.\n\n| Test group | Result | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Functional | skipped | 2 of 3 checks passed. The chat check needs someone signed in, and no sign-in was available. |\n| Context | **passed** | 1 of 1 |\n| Load | **passed** | 1 of 1 |\n| Accessibility | **failed** | The brand colour is too hard to read (details below). The signed-in check was skipped. |\n| Responsiveness | did not run | The run stops at the first failure. |\n\n**Why it failed:** the brand colour is #FFE680, a pale yellow. On a white background it has a contrast of 1.2 to 1. The accessibility standard (WCAG AA) asks for at least 4.5 to 1 so people can read buttons and links. This comes from the colour chosen for the brand, not from a bug in the app's code. The fix is a darker brand colour, or one that doesn't sit on white. That is your choice to make, so I haven't changed anything. A task to track it was filed automatically (mold_v1-009). The full report is at `molds/mold_v1/testing/accessibility/reports/alpha_app-2026-10-09T135939Z.md`.\n\n**Even after the colour is fixed, the run can't fully pass yet.** Three checks need a signed-in session, so they will keep being skipped, and a skipped check can't count as a pass. To get a session, someone who can sign in must be emailed a one-time code. I'll only send that if you tell me to, and tell me which email address to use.\n\nNext steps once you've picked a new colour: re-brand the app, then I'll re-run the tests.",
